  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KfW/DEG - Technical Assistance related to the EFSD+ Guarantee - Green Energy for Africa &amp; Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The EU contribution of up to EUR 25,270,000 (including remuneration) is the Technical Assistance component (hereinafter the &#xbf;&lt;strong&gt;Action&lt;/strong&gt;&#xbf;) of the &lt;strong&gt;&#xbf;Green Energy for Africa and Asia&#xbf; Proposed Investment Program (PIP). &lt;/strong&gt;The &#xbf;Green Energy for Africa and Asia Programme&#xbf; (hereinafter the &#xbf;&lt;strong&gt;Programme&lt;/strong&gt;&#xbf;) comprises of (i) a Technical Assistance component and (ii) a Guarantee component; and was given a positive opinion by the EFSD+ Strategic and Operational Board on 15 December 2022. The Programme is being implemented by Kreditanstalt f&#xfc;r Wiederaufbau (&#xbf;&lt;strong&gt;KfW&lt;/strong&gt;&#xbf;) and KfW DEG (&#xbf;&lt;strong&gt;DEG&lt;/strong&gt;&#xbf;) (hereinafter the &#xbf;&lt;strong&gt;Organisations&lt;/strong&gt;&#xbf;).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Programme seeks to expand access to modern, clean and reliable energy as well as to reduce the share of CO2 emissions of the electricity sector in Sub-Sahara Africa and Asia and furthermore aims to identify and unlock critical raw materials necessary to achieve the 1.5&#xb0; Pathway of the Paris Climate Accords. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Action is supported with a total of up to EUR 25,270,000 as per the following sub-regional funding allocations which should be respected on a best-efforts basis: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sub-Saharan Africa (up to EUR): &lt;/strong&gt;Western Africa: 6,883,333/ Central and Eastern Africa: 6,463,333/ Southern Africa: 4,573,334 &lt;strong&gt;Total: 17,920,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Asia (up to EUR): &lt;/strong&gt;South and East Asia, Southeast Asia : 7,350,000 &lt;strong&gt;Total: 7,350,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
